@startuml
title Activiti 7 Guide-Documented Platform Examples - System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

' ============================================================
' Actors / User Classes
' ============================================================
package "User Classes" {
  actor "Authenticated User" as AuthUser
  actor "Task API User\n(ACTIVITI_USER /\nROLE_ACTIVITI_USER)" as TaskUser
  actor "Human Participant" as HumanPart
  actor "Cluster Operator" as ClusterOp
  actor "Developer / Integrator" as Dev
}

' ============================================================
' External Identity / Security
' ============================================================
package "Identity & Security" {
  component "Keycloak\n(SSO / Identity Provider)" as Keycloak
  component "Spring Boot Application Context" as SpringBoot
  component "Spring Security\n(users, groups, roles,\nlogged-in user context)" as SpringSecurity
}

' ============================================================
' Access / Edge
' ============================================================
package "External Access" {
  component "NGINX Ingress Controller" as Ingress
  component "Public IP" as PublicIP
  component "Gateway / API Gateway\n(architecture background)" as Gateway
}

' ============================================================
' Activiti Cloud Runtime
' ============================================================
package "Activiti Cloud Runtime" {
  component "Example Runtime Bundle\n(deployed process definitions,\nprocess instance execution)" as RuntimeBundle

  component "ProcessRuntime API" as ProcessRuntime
  component "TaskRuntime API\n(requires logged-in user\nwith ACTIVITI_USER)" as TaskRuntime

  component "Audit Service" as AuditService
  component "Query Service\n(process execution info)" as QueryService

  component "Notification Service\n(architecture background)" as NotificationService
  component "Cloud Connectors\n(architecture background)" as CloudConnectors
}

' ============================================================
' Deployment / Infrastructure
' ============================================================
package "Kubernetes / GKE" {
  component "Kubernetes Registry /\nConfig Maps\n(architecture background)" as K8sConfig
  component "Deployment Descriptors\n(input rate,\nreplica counts)" as DeployDescriptors
}

' ============================================================
' Data Items
' ============================================================
database "Authentication Token\n(DE-001, time-limited)" as Token
database "Process Definition Listing\n(DE-002)" as DefListing
database "Process Instance Start Request\n(DE-003)" as StartReq
database "Audit Event Records\n(DE-004)" as AuditEvents
database "Process Execution Information\n(DE-005)" as ExecInfo
database "User Role Information\n(DE-006)" as RoleInfo

' ============================================================
' Relationships - Users and identity
' ============================================================
AuthUser --> Keycloak : acquire token (API-001)
Keycloak --> Token : issues (DR-001)
AuthUser --> Token : supply token (CI-003)

AuthUser --> SpringBoot : requests protected endpoint
SpringBoot --> SpringSecurity : authorization context (CI-001, C-001)
SpringSecurity --> RoleInfo : manages users/groups/roles (DR-006, API-007)
RoleInfo --> TaskUser

Dev --> AuthUser : follows guide examples
Dev --> Dev : documented full example\n(ProcessRuntime + TaskRuntime\n+ human participant) (FR-006)

' ============================================================
' Relationships - External access / ingress
' ============================================================
ClusterOp --> Ingress : configure ingress (FR-007)
ClusterOp --> DeployDescriptors : configure scalability (NFR-002)
PublicIP --> Ingress
Ingress --> AuthUser : routes external requests (CI-002, API-009, C-003)
Ingress --> Gateway : routes into cloud services
Gateway --> ProcessRuntime
Gateway --> TaskRuntime

' ============================================================
' Relationships - Runtime interaction
' ============================================================
Token --> AuthUser : valid token accepted / invalid-rejected (FR-001, NFR-001)
AuthUser --> ProcessRuntime : authenticated API call
AuthUser --> TaskRuntime : authenticated API call

ProcessRuntime --> RuntimeBundle : start / interact (FR-003)
TaskRuntime --> RuntimeBundle : task interaction (FR-005, NFR-003)
TaskRuntime --> SpringSecurity : checks logged-in user + role (C-002, AD-003)

RuntimeBundle --> DefListing : exposes deployed definitions (FR-002, DR-002)
ProcessRuntime --> StartReq : start SimpleProcess (FR-003, DR-003)
StartReq --> RuntimeBundle : creates new instance
RuntimeBundle --> AuditService : just-started instance events
AuditService --> AuditEvents : displays events (FR-004, DR-004, API-005)
RuntimeBundle --> QueryService : process execution state
QueryService --> ExecInfo : exposes info (DR-005, API-006)

HumanPart --> TaskRuntime : participates in process example (API-008)

' ============================================================
' Relationships - Deployment configuration
' ============================================================
DeployDescriptors --> K8sConfig : read parameters
K8sConfig --> RuntimeBundle : scaling / input rate config (NFR-002, DR-007, AD-005)
DeployDescriptors --> CloudConnectors : replica / input rate controls

' ============================================================
' Background components (no assigned functional behavior)
' ============================================================
NotificationService ..> RuntimeBundle : architecture background (C-006)
CloudConnectors ..> RuntimeBundle : architecture background (C-006)

' ============================================================
' Compatibility / scope notes
' ============================================================
note right of SpringBoot
  Compatibility context (C-004):
  Activiti 7.0.0-EA-201802 aligned with
  Spring Boot 2.0.0.RELEASE and
  Spring Cloud Finchley.M8.
  Point-in-time only, not an ongoing
  build obligation for the guide.
end note

note bottom of RuntimeBundle
  Scope (C-005, C-006): Requirements describe
  platform behaviors demonstrated by the guide,
  not a runtime implementation of Activiti,
  Keycloak, Spring Security, or Kubernetes.
  Background components (Gateway, Query,
  Notification, Cloud Connectors, registry/
  config maps) carry no mandatory behavior
  unless assigned by a functional requirement.
end note

@enduml